IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `psga-directions`

-- Public Sector (Governance) Act 2018 (Singapore) -- Part 5 (financial administration), s 42
-- (amending the Schedules) and the transitional rules in s 45 not covered with Part 3.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules
-- skill. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate.

§ `Public Sector (Governance) Act 2018 -- Part 5 and ss 42, 45`

§§ `33 -- who Part 5 applies to, and the Group 1B carve-out`

-- s 33(1): "This Part applies to and in relation to -- (a) every Group 1 public body TO THE EXTENT
-- PROVIDED in this Part; (b) every Group 2 public body; and (c) every GROUP 3B public body."
--
-- GROUP 3A IS NOT NAMED, so Part 5 does not apply to the Group 3A bodies at all. And Group 1 is
-- applied "to the extent provided": ss 37 (auditor), 38 (powers of auditor), 39 (auditor's
-- report), 40 (audited statements) and 41(2) and (3) (presentation of the annual report to
-- Parliament) each exclude GROUP 1B, which is the Defence Science and Technology Agency alone.
-- So the Agency must prepare estimates (s 34), keep accounts (s 36) and report to its Minister
-- (s 41(1)), and is outside the audit regime and the presentation of anything to Parliament.
-- Group 2 here carries the main-function condition (psga-directions.l4); Group 3B does not.
GIVEN `the body` IS A BodyFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Part 5 applies to the body` IF
        `the body is a Group 1 public body` `the body`
    OR  `the body is a Group 2 public body` `the body`
    OR  `the body is a Group 3B public body` `the body`

GIVEN `the body` IS A BodyFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the audit and Parliament provisions apply to the body` IF
        `Part 5 applies to the body` `the body`
    AND NOT `the body is a Group 1B public body` `the body`

-- s 33(2): this Part does not affect (a) any power of the President under the Constitution over
-- the estimates of a Group 1 body in the Fifth Schedule; (b) any power of the responsible
-- Minister under the constitutional Act to approve estimates; or (c) any specific requirement in
-- a constitutional Act delimiting the time or form of estimates, the annual financial statements
-- or the sending of audited statements to the Minister.
GIVEN `the constitutional Act has its own time or form requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the constitutional Act's requirement prevails over Part 5` IF
    `the constitutional Act has its own time or form requirement`

§§ `34, 35 -- estimates`

-- s 34(1): a public body or its governing body "MUST, in every financial year ..., prepare or
-- cause to be prepared, and must ADOPT a statement containing annual estimates of its revenue and
-- expenditure FOR THE FOLLOWING FINANCIAL YEAR." s 34(2): a copy "must, upon their adoption ..., be
-- sent as soon as possible to the responsible Minister".
-- s 35(1): supplementary estimates "MAY" be prepared and adopted during the year; (2) a copy of
-- those adopted must be sent as soon as possible to the Minister.
--
-- Annual estimates are a duty; supplementary estimates a permission. The duty to send applies in
-- both cases once adopted.
DECLARE Estimates HAS
    `the estimates were prepared and adopted during the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `they cover the following financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a copy was sent to the responsible Minister as soon as possible after adoption` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the estimates` IS AN Estimates
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the annual estimates duty in section 34 is met` IF
        `the estimates`'s `the estimates were prepared and adopted during the financial year`
    AND `the estimates`'s `they cover the following financial year`
    AND `the estimates`'s `a copy was sent to the responsible Minister as soon as possible after adoption`

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a public body must prepare supplementary estimates` IF
    FALSE

§§ `36 -- accounts and records`

-- s 36: "A public body must -- (a) keep proper accounts and records of its transactions and
-- affairs and in accordance with the requirements of written law; and (b) do all things
-- necessary to ensure that -- (i) all payments out of its moneys are correctly made and
-- properly authorised; and (ii) adequate control is maintained over the property and assets of,
-- or in the custody of, the public body and over the expenditure incurred by the public body."
DECLARE Controls HAS
    `proper accounts and records are kept in accordance with written law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `all payments out of its moneys are correctly made and properly authorised` IS A BOOLEAN
    `adequate control is maintained over property and assets` IS A BOOLEAN
    `adequate control is maintained over expenditure` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the controls` IS A Controls
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the duties in section 36 are met` IF
        `the controls`'s `proper accounts and records are kept in accordance with written law`
    AND `the controls`'s `all payments out of its moneys are correctly made and properly authorised`
    AND `the controls`'s `adequate control is maintained over property and assets`
    AND `the controls`'s `adequate control is maintained over expenditure`

§§ `37 -- the auditor`

-- s 37(1): "The accounts of a public body must be audited by -- (a) the AUDITOR-GENERAL; or (b)
-- another auditor APPOINTED ANNUALLY BY THE RESPONSIBLE MINISTER for the public body IN
-- CONSULTATION WITH the Auditor-General."
-- s 37(2): "A person is not qualified for appointment as an auditor under subsection (1)(b) unless
-- the person is a PUBLIC ACCOUNTANT who is registered or deemed to be registered under the
-- Accountants Act 2004."
-- s 37(3): the auditor's remuneration "must be paid out of the funds of the public body unless
-- otherwise provided in the constitutional Act".
--
-- The appointment is the MINISTER'S, not the public body's, and it is annual. And the
-- qualification is a public accountant: an individual. The Companies Act 1967 s 10, by contrast,
-- lets an accounting firm, corporation or limited liability partnership be a company's auditor.
-- Under this section a firm as such does not qualify; a public accountant in it would.
DECLARE AuditorAppointment HAS
    `the auditor is the Auditor-General` IS A BOOLEAN
    `appointed by the responsible Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
    `appointed for the year, annually` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in consultation with the Auditor-General` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a public accountant registered or deemed registered under the Accountants Act 2004` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the appointment` IS AN AuditorAppointment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the auditor is validly appointed under section 37` IF
        `the appointment`'s `the auditor is the Auditor-General`
    OR  (    `the appointment`'s `appointed by the responsible Minister`
         AND `the appointment`'s `appointed for the year, annually`
         AND `the appointment`'s `in consultation with the Auditor-General`
         AND `the appointment`'s `a public accountant registered or deemed registered under the Accountants Act 2004`)

GIVEN `the constitutional Act provides otherwise about remuneration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the auditor's remuneration is paid out of the funds of the public body` IF
    NOT `the constitutional Act provides otherwise about remuneration`

§§ `38 -- the auditor's powers, and the offence`

-- s 38(1): a public body "must, as soon as practicable after the close of each financial year but
-- not later than the time (if any) delimited in its constitutional Act, prepare and submit the
-- financial statements ... to the auditor ..., who must audit and report on them."
-- s 38(2): the auditor, or a person the auditor authorises, "is entitled at all reasonable times
-- -- (a) to full and free access to all accounting and other records ...; (b) to make copies of
-- or take extracts from any of those ...; and (c) to require any person to furnish ... any
-- information in the possession of that person, or to which that person has access, that the
-- auditor ... considers necessary".
-- s 38(3): "A person -- (a) who, WITHOUT ANY REASONABLE CAUSE, fails to comply with any
-- requirement of the auditor ... under subsection (2); or (b) who otherwise HINDERS, OBSTRUCTS OR
-- DELAYS the auditor ... in the performance of his or her functions ... shall be guilty of an
-- offence and shall be liable on conviction to a FINE NOT EXCEEDING $1,000."
--
-- The offence is open to "a person", not only to the public body or its officers, and the penalty
-- is a fine only, at a fifth of the level of the s 7 offences. Limb (a) has the reasonable-cause
-- escape; limb (b) has none.
`the maximum fine under section 38(3), in dollars` MEANS 1000

DECLARE ObstructionFacts HAS
    `the auditor or an authorised person made a requirement under section 38(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person failed to comply with it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person had reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person otherwise hindered, obstructed or delayed the auditor in performing functions or exercising powers` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS AN ObstructionFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 38(3) is committed` IF
        (    `the facts`'s `the auditor or an authorised person made a requirement under section 38(2)`
         AND `the facts`'s `the person failed to comply with it`
         AND NOT `the facts`'s `the person had reasonable cause`)
    OR  `the facts`'s `the person otherwise hindered, obstructed or delayed the auditor in performing functions or exercising powers`

§§ `39 -- the auditor's report`

-- s 39(1): the report "must state -- (a) whether the financial statements show fairly the
-- financial transactions and the state of affairs of the public body; (b) whether proper
-- accounting and other records have been kept, including records of all assets ... whether
-- purchased, donated or otherwise; (c) whether the receipts, expenditure, investment of moneys, and
-- the acquisition and disposal of assets ... have been in accordance with this Act, the
-- constitutional Act and the requirements of any other written law applicable to moneys of or
-- managed by the public body; and (d) any other matters arising from the audit that the auditor
-- considers should be reported."
-- s 39(2): the auditor must send the report to the public body as soon as practicable.
-- s 39(3): the auditor "may at any other time report to the responsible Minister ... THROUGH THE
-- PUBLIC BODY upon any matter arising out of the performance of an audit".
--
-- Even the auditor's direct line to the Minister runs through the body being audited.
DECLARE ReportContent HAS
    `says whether the statements show fairly the transactions and state of affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
    `says whether proper accounting and other records were kept, including records of all assets` IS A BOOLEAN
    `says whether receipts, expenditure, investments and dealings in assets were in accordance with the Act, the constitutional Act and other written law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reports any other matter arising from the audit that the auditor considers should be reported` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the report` IS A ReportContent
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the report states what section 39(1) requires` IF
        `the report`'s `says whether the statements show fairly the transactions and state of affairs`
    AND `the report`'s `says whether proper accounting and other records were kept, including records of all assets`
    AND `the report`'s `says whether receipts, expenditure, investments and dealings in assets were in accordance with the Act, the constitutional Act and other written law`

-- The fourth head is "any other matters ... the auditor considers should be reported": it
-- requires the auditor to report what the auditor thinks should be reported and nothing more, so
-- it is not a condition of the report stating what (a) to (c) require.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the auditor may report to the Minister without passing the report through the public body` IF
    FALSE

§§ `40, 41 -- reaching the Minister, and Parliament`

-- s 40(1): the public body must, "as soon as its accounts and financial statements have been
-- audited", send the Minister "a copy of the audited financial statements, SIGNED BY THE
-- CHAIRPERSON of the public body, together with a copy of the auditor's report under s 39(1)."
-- s 40(2): "Where the auditor of a public body is NOT THE AUDITOR-GENERAL, the auditor must forward a
-- copy ... to the Auditor-General AT THE SAME TIME they are submitted to the public body."
-- s 40(3): the Minister "must, AS SOON AS PRACTICABLE, cause a copy ... to be presented to
-- Parliament." No deadline is stated.
-- s 41(1): the body must, "as soon as practicable after the end of each financial year", cause a
-- report on its activities to be prepared and sent to the Minister, containing such information
-- as the Minister may direct. s 41(2): the Minister must cause a copy to be presented to Parliament.
-- s 41(3): s 41(2) does not apply to a Group 1B body.
DECLARE Reporting HAS
    `the audited statements were sent to the responsible Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
    `signed by the chairperson` IS A BOOLEAN
    `with the auditor's report under section 39(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the auditor is the Auditor-General` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a non-Auditor-General auditor forwarded a copy to the Auditor-General at the same time as submitting to the public body` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the reporting` IS A Reporting
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the audited statements were sent as section 40(1) requires` IF
        `the reporting`'s `the audited statements were sent to the responsible Minister`
    AND `the reporting`'s `signed by the chairperson`
    AND `the reporting`'s `with the auditor's report under section 39(1)`

GIVEN `the reporting` IS A Reporting
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Auditor-General has been given a copy as section 40(2) requires` IF
        `the reporting`'s `the auditor is the Auditor-General`
    OR  `the reporting`'s `a non-Auditor-General auditor forwarded a copy to the Auditor-General at the same time as submitting to the public body`

GIVEN `the body` IS A BodyFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister must present the audited statements to Parliament` IF
    `the audit and Parliament provisions apply to the body` `the body`

GIVEN `the body` IS A BodyFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister must present the annual report to Parliament` IF
    `the audit and Parliament provisions apply to the body` `the body`

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act sets a deadline for presenting to Parliament` IF
    FALSE

§§ `42 -- amending the Schedules`

-- s 42(1): "The Minister may, by order in the Gazette, add, delete or replace any public body in any
-- of the Schedules."
-- s 42(2): "However, nothing in subsection (1) authorises adding the MONETARY AUTHORITY OF SINGAPORE
-- to any of the Schedules."
--
-- The Minister can move any body into or out of any Group by order, and with it into or out of the
-- chief-executive controls, the conflict regime and the audit regime, with one named exception. The
-- exception is express, which means the Monetary Authority of Singapore is the one body the Act
-- contemplates being kept out of its governance framework by name.
DECLARE ScheduleOrder IS ONE OF
    `adds a body`
    `deletes a body`
    `replaces a body`

GIVEN `the order` IS A ScheduleOrder, `the body added is the Monetary Authority of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 42 authorises the order` IF
    CONSIDER `the order`
    WHEN `deletes a body` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `adds a body` THEN NOT `the body added is the Monetary Authority of Singapore`
    WHEN `replaces a body` THEN NOT `the body added is the Monetary Authority of Singapore`

§§ `45 -- saving and transitional`

-- s 45(1): "Any direction made or given before 1 April 2018 by a responsible Minister to a public body
-- under the constitutional Act ... continues in force and is to be treated, on or after that date,
-- as if made or given under section 5."
-- s 45(5): Part 4 does not affect (a) any meeting of which notice was given before 1 April 2018 and
-- which was not held or was adjourned immediately before that date, which "may be continued ... as
-- if this Act had not been enacted"; or (b) the continued operation or validity of any order or
-- decision made before that date, which is treated as made under the corresponding provisions.
-- s 45(6): every chief executive, officer or employee of a public body immediately before 1 April
-- 2018 continues to hold office as if appointed under the constitutional Act as amended by this Act.
--
-- Because an old direction is treated as a s 5 direction, an old direction to a Group 2 or Group 3
-- body, which s 5 cannot reach, is treated as made under a power that body is outside. The Act does
-- not say what becomes of it.
GIVEN `the direction was made or given before 1 April 2018` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `it was given by a responsible Minister to a public body under the constitutional Act or another written law the body administers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the direction continues in force as if given under section 5` IF
        `the direction was made or given before 1 April 2018`
    AND `it was given by a responsible Minister to a public body under the constitutional Act or another written law the body administers`

GIVEN `the body` IS A BodyFacts,
      `the direction was made or given before 1 April 2018` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a saved pre-2018 direction is to a body a section 5 direction can reach` IF
        `the direction was made or given before 1 April 2018`
    AND `the body is a Group 1 public body` `the body`
